{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>My threshed.</b> Now Babylon is a threshing floor, and the yod is a sign of the name or of the prophet, or it is a construct form, for 'even I threshed her' and she was like a son of the threshing floor. It is possible that 'son of the threshing floor' is the grain that remains, and this is an allusion to Israel."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:29.143838258Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}